ols from keeping a student's education record from their parents. It also bars changing a student's gender identity on that record without the parents' written consent.\n- **Why it's blank:** The bill puts McCay on the side of involving parents, but it doesn't pick one rung on that side.\n  - It never says schools must notify parents on their own (rung 4).\n  - What it governs is the education record, not staff using a different name or pronouns (rung 5). The codebook's rule that the rung's object must match (H17) keeps it from counting as rung 5.\n  - Its consent requirement goes beyond rung 3, which only asks schools to tell parents when parents ask.\n- **What the row records:**\n  - **Vote page:** `actor_quote` \"Kennedy, M. McCay, D. McKell, M.\" and `tally_quote` \"Yeas 22 Nays 6 Abs 1\".\n  - **Bill text:** the consent clause as `provision_quote`.\n  - **Blank fields:** `rests_on` is empty and there are no quotes, because none of the sources contain McCay's own words.\n- **`needs_source`:** McCay's own words on telling parents about a student's gender identity, and any later Senate roll call of his on a bill that requires notifying parents or getting their consent.","ttft_ms":9414,"type":"result","duration_ms":25800,"uuid":"e98acaac-0f04-4006-a009-2cfccd72ba46","ttft_stream_ms":1122,"time_to_request_ms":76,"first_content_frame_ms":1122,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
